+## Play a live game
+
+Prepare a quiz in `/moderate`, then choose **Start a game**. Each click creates
+an independent game and opens its moderator big screen. Share the full join URL
+or display its locally generated QR code. Players enter **Your name** and press
+**Join**; no account is needed. Their browser remembers them for that game.
+
+Use **Start**, **Finish**, **Next**, and finally **End quiz**. Phones and counters
+update live without reloads. Players can change their selection until **Finish**;
+only their last selection counts. Correct answers are never sent to players
+before the question closes. Late joining is allowed until the game ends.
+
+Only active questions are copied into a game, in quiz order. Quiz edits do not
+change games already created. A **Games** list on the quiz page lets moderators
+return to an existing big screen after a restart. Game state, players, and
+answers persist in SQLite. An empty game ends safely when started.
+
+Active-player counts use live connections and heartbeat leases, with a short
+Wi-Fi reconnection grace period; closed tabs are removed after about 8–10 seconds,
+and silently unreachable devices expire after at most 35–37 seconds. Rejoining
+restores the same player and their answers. [Protocol/design notes](docs/live-games.md).
+
